  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Raja Vocative** (1 review): Track thirteen is Raja Vocative, from the Orange Raja 7-inch, not Blood Royal [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The Ballad of Bull Ramos**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Deuteronomy**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Beyond the Mysterious Beyond**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Raja Vocative**: back after 58 archived shows (2127 days) [3]\n- **Song for Dennis Brown**: back after 30 archived shows (1023 days) [3]\n- **The Legend of Chavo Guerrero**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **/piano jam**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Luna [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2015-04-11.citywinery_acidjack** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 94 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The audio quality of the recording is described as flawless [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John Darnielle played vocals, guitar, and keys; Matt Douglas played sax, guitar, and horns [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2015-04-11.citywinery_acidjack**: taped by acidjack; transferred by acidjack; source: Digital Matrix [1]. Also: Recorded by Brandon Eggleston using Schoeps MK41 mics and a Sound Devices USBPre2; Processed in Adobe Audition, Izotope Ozone, and Audacity, then encoded as FLAC level 8 [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Themes: [The Mountain Goats: April 11, 2015 City Winery – FLAC/MP3/Streaming | nyctaper](https://www.nyctaper.com/2015/04/the-mountain-goats-april-11-2015-city-winery-flacmp3streaming/) [4]",
